<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχμᾰλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rolled stone, pebble,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.6.4
			</span></i>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχμαλοι,</span>
			<i>a heap of such stones, cobble-wall, dry dyke,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1259.33
			</span></i>; also neut. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχμαλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					143
				</span></i>
			: sg. in collect. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆμα χωστῷ τροχμάλῳ κατηρεφές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1064
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
